{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.82,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U2", "C1"],
      "pins": ["U2.28", "C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U2-VCC)", "VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "The SSD1306/OLED part U2 has pin 28 named VCC with pintype power_in, but it is not connected to the global VCC rail. It appears only on the local net Net-(U2-VCC), together with C1 pin 1; C1 pin 2 is GND. The global VCC net includes U2 pins 6, 9, and 11, but not U2 pin 28.",
      "expected": "A power_in supply pin such as SSD1306 VCC should be connected to the board VCC rail, with C1 serving as its decoupling capacitor. The specification identifies U4 VCC as a supply pin: \"C7 (2.2 µF) — U4 VCC (digital-logic supply pin) to GND\".",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"22\") (name \"Net-(U2-VCC)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C1\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"28\") (pinfunction \"VCC\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"VCC\") (class \"Default\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"BS1\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")) ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"28\") (name \"VCC\") (type \"power_in\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C7 (2.2 µF) — U4 `VCC` (digital-logic supply pin) to GND"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The SSD1306 VCC/analog supply pin is left floating except for a capacitor to ground. This can prevent the OLED driver from powering up correctly or make the display nonfunctional, even though VDD and VBAT are connected to VCC.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design is otherwise consistent with the Portal specification, but the OLED/SSD1306 VCC supply pin is not tied to the global VCC rail, leaving a power_in pin floating; this is a likely functional anomaly."
}

